# benchmark output: trial repos and raw results are large and machine-specific.
# The published REPORT.md is committed by hand when a sweep is worth quoting.
# The glob (not just evals/results/) matters: a sweep against a private repo
# writes to evals/results-private/, whose work/ holds full copies of that repo.
evals/results*/
# same for the design benchmark, whose work/ holds every arm's raw transcript
# and _plans/ holds the generated plans
evals/design/results*/

# benchmark tasks that point at private or proprietary repos. These are for
# local validation only — they can never be part of a published benchmark
# (a reader can't reproduce them), and their patches quote closed source.
evals/tasks-private/

# local design/handover material — kept on disk, not in the repo
Arch Canvas Handover.pdf
Arch harness React redesign/
docs/
_demo_reverse_seed.py

# design-benchmark tasks pointing at the proprietary A2V2 repo. Local validation
# only — a reader cannot reproduce them and the trap text quotes closed source.
evals/design/tasks-private/
